Path handling for the S3 API listener only (sectionName). S3 SigV4 signs the
request path byte for byte, so Envoy's two default rewrites break any key that
contains an empty path segment or an encoded slash:

  disableMergeSlashes: true   -> '/bucket/a//b.pdf' is forwarded as signed
                                 instead of collapsing to '/bucket/a/b.pdf'
  escapedSlashesAction:
    KeepUnchanged             -> '/bucket/a%2Fb.pdf' is forwarded as signed
                                 instead of 307-redirecting

Scoped to one listener because ClientTrafficPolicy path settings are per
listener: applying them to 'https' or 'https-apex' would relax normalization for
the UI, API and keycloak routes as well.

Not covered: Envoy's normalize_path (dot-segment resolution, '/x/../y'). Gateway
API exposes no field for it - the only lever is an EnvoyPatchPolicy, which this
installer deliberately does not use. Keys containing '..' are rejected by the
data-prep service before they are signed.
#}
apiVersion: gateway.envoyproxy.io/v1alpha1
kind: ClientTrafficPolicy
metadata:
  name: {{ (gateway_name ~ '-s3-path') | to_json }}
  namespace: {{ gateway_namespace | to_json }}
spec:
  targetRefs:
    - group: gateway.networking.k8s.io
      kind: Gateway
      name: {{ gateway_name | to_json }}
      sectionName: {{ gateway_s3_listener_name | to_json }}
  path:
    disableMergeSlashes: true
    escapedSlashesAction: KeepUnchanged
